WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.005
Why build diverse research teams?

2
00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:07.723
Because diversity makes research stronger.

3
00:00:08.473 --> 00:00:12.548
Team members with different backgrounds bring varied lenses to a problem.

4
00:00:13.298 --> 00:00:17.437
They uncover blind spots and assumptions that others take for granted.

5
00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:21.792
They enhance creativity by combining ideas in new ways.

6
00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:26.937
And their findings tend to be more widely applicable and more widely cited.

7
00:00:27.687 --> 00:00:30.588
Inclusive teams start with inclusive recruitment.

8
00:00:30.938 --> 00:00:38.123
Before recruiting, define diversity and inclusion goals, remove biased language and unnecessary requirements,

9
00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:42.671
plan outreach to diverse networks, and set up a diverse hiring panel.

10
00:00:43.421 --> 00:00:50.317
During recruitment, advertise widely, offer flexible application formats, and use standardised interview

11
00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:55.091
questions focused on skills and competencies, not on cultural fit alone.

12
00:00:55.841 --> 00:01:00.923
After recruitment, document diversity outcomes where legally appropriate, review the

13
00:01:00.923 --> 00:01:05.825
process for barriers, and provide onboarding that highlights inclusive practices.

